    {"id":"legend","type":"text","x":50,"y":1100,"width":1500,"height":240,"text":"Blue: local Private Link worker paths; vault-to-Event Grid arrows are platform publishing.\nOrange dashed: Event Grid trusted-service delivery / dead-letter exception; Microsoft backbone, NOT Private Link.\nGray dashed: inactive standby or reverse path; fence the old writer and worker before manual promotion.\nEach regional VNet has private endpoints to BOTH vaults. No inter-region VNet peering required. 18 PEs total.\nPrivate app/SCM publication requires a connected workstation or runner; ARM management remains separate.\nOnly current secret state is synchronized; no automatic delete/purge, keys, certificates, or historical mirroring.","fontSize":16,"fontFamily":2,"strokeColor":"#000000","textAlign":"left","verticalAlign":"top"}
